# Every variable below, where it is read and what breaks without it: docs/configuration.md.
# Copy to .env.local (gitignored). Datasets on this machine the dev server offers on the Datasets page:
# label=absolute path, separated by ';'. Conversation atlases (the atlas pipeline's output) load as entities.
# A directory entry (a ChatGPT data export) serves its conversations*.json files; with an atlas entry beside it the page offers loading both, linked.
# AEGRAPH_LOCAL_DEMOS="ChatGPT atlas=/path/to/conversation-atlas.nodocs.json;ChatGPT conversations=/path/to/chatgpt-export"

# Voice on this machine: the dev server serves /api/openai (ungated, loopback, this page only — dev/openai.ts) with
# this key, so the assistant's listener and speaker use OpenAI's models locally with nothing else to set up. Without
# it the browser's own recogniser and voice are used. The chat is Claude Code over the bridge locally, always.
# A deployed copy is a static site and reads no variable: there, a user's own keys go in the assistant settings.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# AEGRAPH_FEATURES_OFF=         features this build leaves out, comma-separated: maps, globe, videos, audio (default none)

# ── The Claude Code bridge (mcp/server.mjs, on each developer's machine) ─────────────────────────
# AEGRAPH_BRIDGE_ORIGINS=       comma-separated page origins allowed to connect, replacing the default
#                               (any localhost / 127.0.0.1 page, plus the hosted origin below). A company: its own origin.
# AEGRAPH_HOSTED_ORIGIN=https://your.site   the one hosted site trusted besides this machine's pages (unset: https://aegraph.sh; empty: none)
# AEGRAPH_BRIDGE_TOKEN=         a token the tab must present (set the same in the app's bridge settings); default none
# AEGRAPH_BRIDGE_PORT=8787      the first port the bridge tries
# AEGRAPH_BRIDGE_PORT_SPAN=10   how many ports after it to try when it is taken
# AEGRAPH_BRIDGE_TIMEOUT_MS=120000  how long one tool call may take
# AEGRAPH_BRIDGE_WAIT_MS=8000   how long a call waits for a tab to connect
# AEGRAPH_CLAUDE_BIN=claude     the Claude Code binary the in-app chat runs
# AEGRAPH_CLAUDE_ARGS=          extra arguments for it (a model, a setting — never a permission; those are dropped)
# AEGRAPH_CLAUDE_LINGER_MS=5000 how long an idle chat process is kept
# (AEGRAPH_BRIDGE_CHAT and AEGRAPH_BRIDGE_FOR_TAB are set by the bridge for its own chat child; do not set them.)

# ── The headless engine (npm run headless: the app's tools over MCP, no browser) ────────────────
# AEGRAPH_WORKSPACE=            the workspace file it opens (or the first argument)
# AEGRAPH_HEADLESS_PORT=        serve over HTTP on this loopback port instead of stdio
# AEGRAPH_HEADLESS_TOKEN=       the bearer token HTTP clients must send (default: a random one, printed at start)
# AEGRAPH_HEADLESS_CONFIRM=     allow | refuse — destructive tools over HTTP (default refuse; stdio allows)

# ── The demos the build copies in (scripts/demos/fetch.mjs, vite.config.ts) ─────────────────────
# AEGRAPH_DEMOS_DIR=            a checkout of aegraph-ui-demos on this machine (default ../aegraph-ui-demos)
# AEGRAPH_DEMOS_REPO=adrewh2/aegraph-ui-demos   or the repo to fetch them from
# AEGRAPH_DEMOS_REF=main        the branch, tag or commit — pin a commit for a reproducible build
# AEGRAPH_DEMOS_TOKEN=          a GitHub token that can read that repo (it is private)
# AEGRAPH_DEMOS_SITE=https://aegraph.dev   with neither, the demos a site publishes (`off` for none)
# AEGRAPH_DEMOS_LIVE=0          stop the dev server serving the checkout's demos live
